note fuel_while: a while with no bound has fuel 1000000 (front.om fe_lwhile, omc S_WHILE): the 1000000th
note pass ends with i = 1000000 and the next head traps 4 (exit 104); a lowering with one pass more
note writes the line below first, so stdout differs.
text hit "pass 1000001\n"
fn main to int
i = ulong 0
while lt i 2000000
i = add i 1
if eq i 1000001
k = write 1 hit 0 len hit
end
end
ret int and i 255
end
